          "date": "2026-10-17 22:55:42.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-11962 lod: prepare for a SOM mirror in FLR files",
        "message": "LU-11962 lod: prepare for a SOM mirror in FLR files\n\nStrict Size-on-MDT of files that are not mirrored will use a mirror\nmade of a single data-less foreign HSM component flagged HS_SOM, so\nthat clients send a layout write intent before they modify the file.\nPrepare servers and utilities to handle files with such a mirror:\n\n- move the code that appends an HSM mirror to a layout out of\n  lod_declare_pccro_set() into lod_layout_add_hsm_mirror();\n- define HS_SOM, shown as \"som\" by \"lfs getstripe\";\n- clear the stale flag of a SOM component at RESYNC_DONE, as it has\n  no data to resync, and accept its ID in the list of resynced ones;\n- copy no data into a SOM mirror in llapi_mirror_resync_many(), and\n  read from no foreign mirror in llapi_mirror_find(), so \"lfs mirror\n  resync\" makes such a file RDONLY again;\n- do not reuse a SOM mirror as the HSM mirror of PCC-RO.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-flr,sanity-pcc\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I28ceb8221a6402dfd69362989e9705ccb85056a8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
